### VS Code REST Client examples for Events API
# Requires the app running on http://localhost:8082

### 1) List events (default pagination: _limit=3, _page=1)
GET http://localhost:8082/events
Accept: application/json

### 2) List events with explicit pagination
GET http://localhost:8082/events?_limit=5&_page=1
Accept: application/json

### 3) Search events by title/description/organizer name (with pagination)
GET http://localhost:8082/events?title=music&_limit=5&_page=1
Accept: application/json

### 4) Get event by id
GET http://localhost:8082/events/1
Accept: application/json

### 5) Create a new event
# Note: organizer id must exist; images can be object keys or full URLs
POST http://localhost:8082/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "category": "Music",
  "title": "Jazz Night",
  "description": "Live jazz session",
  "location": "Bangkok",
  "date": "2025-10-20",
  "time": "20:00",
  "petAllowed": true,
  "organizer": { "id": 1 },
  "images": [
    "events/example-1.jpg",
    "https://picsum.photos/seed/event-1/400/300"
  ]
}
